	(footprint "aiee:SOIC-8-EP_LM5017_TI-MRA08B"
		(locked yes)
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "aa34d5cd-287e-4820-89e9-0db067b35872")
		(at 50.25 85.25)
		(descr "LM5017 SO PowerPAD-8 (TI DDA0008B), land pattern TI MRA08B Rev B, datasheet p.29. NAME IS STALE: the exposed pad is now 3.10 x 2.41mm (TI's recommended land, read off the RECOMMENDED LAND PATTERN drawing: (.122)[3.1] along the 1.27mm pitch axis, (.095)[2.41] along the 5.56mm row-span axis), NOT the 2.0 x 2.0mm the filename and the easyeda2kicad pull claim - the pulled EP was 46% undersized in area. 8 leads left as pulled (1.27mm pitch, 5.54mm row span, verified against TI's 1.27 / 5.56). 4 thermal vias 0.30mm drill / 0.61mm pad (0.155mm annulus, above the 0.15mm JLC floor) respread to +/-0.85, +/-0.65 under the enlarged EP; they are NUMBERED 9, i.e. they belong to the EXPOSED PAD net (P7 fix): as netless copper they raised 4 solder_mask_bridge errors (a no-net hole inside pad 9's mask aperture) and 4 clearance errors against pad 9 at 0.25 mm, and both classes vanish once they carry the EP net, which is also what an EP thermal via IS. Their *.Paste and *.Mask layers are REMOVED so they are tented on both faces - mandatory on this board because the bottom copper is a flat heatsink mounting face and a mask-opened via there would take solder and break flatness; tenting is also the standard anti-wicking mitigation for via-in-pad. EP paste aperture reduced 0.20mm per side (2.70 x 2.01 = 73% of the EP) against float/voiding. Courtyard corrected - the pull shipped one that cut through the lead pads.")
		(property "Reference" "U101"
			(at -3.615 0.5 90)
			(layer "F.SilkS")
			(uuid "f080031b-c66a-4dca-a3c9-6fde313832c3")
