		(uuid "b11a3a14-e513-4d81-a316-0a700156a722")
		(at 38.135 62.235)
		(descr "EPC2019 200V eGaN bare die, 7 solder bars. Geometry re-derived from the EPC2019 datasheet RECOMMENDED LAND PATTERN (p.6) by measuring the drawing's own vector geometry, not the dimension labels. VERIFIED SYMMETRIC end to end: BOTH end columns (pins 1/2 and pins 6/7) are 0.45mm centre-to-centre (dim h). The 680/700um figures on that page are the OUTER envelope of an end column (450 + 230 mask = 680; 450 + 250 bump = 700 = dim c = bar-pad length), NOT a column-1 centre spacing. Cross-check: (B - h)/2 = (950-450)/2 = 250 = dim i, the die-edge-to-pad-centre offset, which only closes if h applies to both ends. Copper = bump size (0.25 dia round / 0.25x0.70 bar); solder-mask-defined land, mask 10um smaller per side (-0.01 margin) giving the datasheet's 0.23 / 0.23x0.68 openings. NO VIA IN PAD - 0.23-0.25mm lands admit no drill + annular ring. Pin 7 SUBSTRATE must be netted to SOURCE.")
